# x64echo — vtable-redirect exclusion list (codegen policy DATA, not compiler source)
#
# One fully-qualified BASE class name per line ('#' starts a comment). A class that
# is, or derives from, any base listed here keeps its NATIVE vtable in both worlds:
# it is NOT C-1-redirected to the face vtable, and the backend pass does not stub its
# virtuals. Use this for host-internal polymorphic types that uninstrumented runtime
# code (libstdc++ &c.) dispatches on DIRECTLY from host context -- redirecting those
# makes the raw virtual call cross to the guest and crash.
#
# The compiler holds only the generic mechanism (walk base classes, match this list,
# read via ECHO_NOREDIRECT_FILE). Adding an entry needs no clang rebuild.
#
# std::locale facets: virtual-deleted by std::locale teardown inside libstdc++
# (e.g. muParser's change_dec_sep : std::numpunct, installed in a static std::locale).
std::locale::facet

# Qt's resource registry root: an anonymous-namespace, all-inline-virtual (no key
# function) type QtCore dispatches on directly host-side while resolving a QResource
# (e.g. reading the embedded :/qt/etc/qt.conf during QLibraryInfo init). A bare leaf
# name matches it (its qualified name carries an unstable anonymous-namespace prefix).
QResourceRoot

# Qt's system-locale backend: its virtual query() reads the HOST OS locale, so it must
# run host-side. Redirecting its vtable makes updateSystemPrivate()'s host-side query()
# reenter the guest during QLocale construction and crash. Host-internal; guest never
# subclasses it.
QSystemLocale

# std::thread's internal state object: the std::thread constructor hands a
# _State_impl<...> to libstdc++'s execute_native_thread_routine, which virtual-calls
# _M_run() DIRECTLY, on a host thread, from code Echo never compiled. Redirecting that
# vtable makes the host thread jump into x86 bytes: a background thread (named e.g.
# "rocksdb:low") takes SIGILL at a PC inside the guest address range, with not one
# symbol on the stack -- the host unwinder cannot read guest frames. Host-internal;
# the guest never subclasses it. Any library that uses std::thread hits this.
std::thread::_State
